# Step 25, a follow-up to the rename: the core's test of a command's
# environment read `PATH` from the model's copy of the output, whose long
# line is cut, and now reads the whole output
# (docs/steps/25/parts/pr1c-windows-path.md). The breaks show that the test
# now sees the whole of a `PATH` longer than a line, as it was given: its
# end, its first entry, its order and its repeats. Each runs `cineris-core`'s
# tests only, where the test is; `cineris-tools`' unit tests of
# `absolute_entries` give it four entries at most.

[break] path-loses-what-follows-its-first-entries
rule: `PATH` keeps every absolute directory it was given, in order, however long it is: only the empty and relative entries are dropped.
file: crates/cineris-tools/src/shell/env.rs
in: absolute_entries
find: .collect();
replace: .take(32).collect();
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it shell::sys_a_command_is_given_the_environment_the_command_analysis_relies_on

[break] path-loses-its-first-entry
rule: `PATH` keeps its first absolute directory: only the empty and relative entries are dropped.
file: crates/cineris-tools/src/shell/env.rs
in: absolute_entries
find: .collect();
replace: .skip(1).collect();
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it shell::sys_a_command_is_given_the_environment_the_command_analysis_relies_on

[break] path-put-in-order
rule: `PATH` keeps the order it was given in, which is the order programs are looked for in.
file: crates/cineris-tools/src/shell/env.rs
in: absolute_entries
find: OsString::from(kept.join(&separator.to_string()))
replace:
    {
        let mut kept = kept;
        kept.sort_unstable();
        OsString::from(kept.join(&separator.to_string()))
    }
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it shell::sys_a_command_is_given_the_environment_the_command_analysis_relies_on

[break] path-repeats-taken-out
rule: `PATH` keeps a directory it names twice: nothing but the empty and relative entries is dropped.
file: crates/cineris-tools/src/shell/env.rs
in: absolute_entries
find: OsString::from(kept.join(&separator.to_string()))
replace:
    {
        let mut kept = kept;
        kept.dedup();
        OsString::from(kept.join(&separator.to_string()))
    }
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it shell::sys_a_command_is_given_the_environment_the_command_analysis_relies_on
